IMPORT prelude

-- Fisheries Act 1966 (Singapore) -- who is a fish dealer (s 2), the officer who will not identify himself (s 5(2)), licence
-- validity and partnership licences (ss 7, 8), the poison and explosives offences and their presumption (s 10), trawl-nets
-- (s 12), the general and continuing penalties (s 13), proceeds of seized fish (s 15), liability of partners, employers and
-- officers (ss 17, 19, 20), composition (s 18), offences outside territorial waters (s 22) and exemptions (s 25).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FA1966.txt. The deposit
-- says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest amending Acts annotated in the text are
-- Act 11 of 2019 (Singapore Food Agency Act 2019) and Act 15 of 2019 (Criminal Law Reform Act 2019, s 12(2)).
-- The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body (s 19 to s 22 are misaligned); the body's
-- numbering is followed.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the offences, penalties and the
-- liability rules a fisherman, fish farmer or fish dealer meets. Not encoded: administration and appointments (ss 3, 4), the
-- licensing discretion and appeal (s 6), wilful damage (s 9) and illegal landing (s 11) beyond their penalty, forfeiture and
-- confiscation (ss 14, 16), court jurisdiction (s 21), officers' powers (s 23), service (s 24), fees (s 26) and the rule-making
-- power (s 27). Almost all the operative fishing controls are left by s 27 to rules, none of which were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Fisheries Act 1966 -- offences`

§§ `2 -- fish dealer`

-- s 2: "fish dealer" includes "any person engaged in buying (except for personal consumption), selling, exposing for sale,
-- consigning or exhibiting fish, whether living, fresh or processed, in any manner, or any person engaged in processing fish".
-- "fish" includes crustacea, aquatic mollusca, turtles, marine sponges, trepang "and any other form of aquatic life and the young
-- and eggs thereof".
DECLARE FishActivity IS ONE OF
    `buying fish to eat at home`
    `buying fish for resale`
    `selling fish`
    `exhibiting ornamental fish`
    `curing or freezing fish`
    `catching fish`

GIVEN `the activity` IS A FishActivity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity makes one a fish dealer` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `buying fish to eat at home` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `catching fish` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5(2) -- the officer who will not identify himself`

-- s 5(1): an authorised officer exercising powers must "(a) if not in uniform, declare his office; and (b) on demand, produce ...
-- such identification card as the Director-General may direct".
-- s 5(2): "It shall not be an offence for any person to refuse to comply with any request, demand or order made or given by any
-- authorised officer, or by any police officer not in uniform, who fails to declare his office and refuses to produce his
-- identification card on demand being made by that person."
-- Both failures are needed ("and"). INFERENCE: an officer in uniform has no duty to declare under s 5(1)(a), so the excuse is
-- encoded as available only against an officer not in uniform.
GIVEN `the officer was in uniform` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer declared his office` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person demanded the card` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer produced the card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing the officer is not an offence` IF
        (NOT `the officer was in uniform`)
    AND (NOT `the officer declared his office`)
    AND `the person demanded the card`
    AND (NOT `the officer produced the card`)

§§ `7, 8 -- validity of licences`

-- s 7(1): valid "only for the period, place or purpose specified"; (2): "shall expire on 31 December of the year in which it is
-- issued, unless the contrary is stated in the licence"; (3): "shall not be transferable".
-- s 8(4): "A licence issued to 2 or more persons shall not expire upon the death or retirement from business of any one or more
-- of the partners."
GIVEN `year issued` IS A NUMBER, `year now` IS A NUMBER, `the licence states another expiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence has expired under section 7(2)` IF
    (NOT `the licence states another expiry`) AND `year now` GREATER THAN `year issued`

GIVEN `issued to 2 or more partners` IS A BOOLEAN, `a partner has died or retired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the death or retirement ends the licence` IF
    `a partner has died or retired` AND (NOT `issued to 2 or more partners`)

§§ `10 -- poisons and explosives`

-- s 10(1): "Any person who, except under the authority of a licence ..., uses any poisonous or explosive substance with intent to
-- stupefy, poison or kill fish shall be guilty of an offence."
GIVEN `used poison or explosive` IS A BOOLEAN, `intended to stupefy, poison or kill fish` IS A BOOLEAN, `held a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under section 10(1)` IF
    `used poison or explosive` AND `intended to stupefy, poison or kill fish` AND (NOT `held a licence`)

-- s 10(2): found in possession of fish "captured with the aid of any poisonous or explosive substance and does not give a
-- satisfactory account as to how he came to be in possession thereof". There is no licence exception in (2).
GIVEN `possessed fish caught with poison or explosive` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave a satisfactory account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the possession of fish is an offence under section 10(2)` IF
    `possessed fish caught with poison or explosive` AND (NOT `gave a satisfactory account`)

-- s 10(3): substance found in possession or control "in the neighbourhood of any waters shortly after the use of such a substance
-- in the waters" -- "presumed until the contrary is proved to have made use of the substance for those purposes".
GIVEN `found with the substance near the waters` IS A BOOLEAN, `shortly after its use in the waters` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is taken to have used the substance` IF
    `found with the substance near the waters` AND `shortly after its use in the waters` AND (NOT `proved the contrary`)

-- s 10(4): "Any person in a fishing boat who is found to be in possession or control of any poisonous or explosive substance
-- without a licence shall be guilty of an offence." No intent is required.
GIVEN `in a fishing boat` IS A BOOLEAN, `had poison or explosive` IS A BOOLEAN, `held a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the possession on a fishing boat is an offence under section 10(4)` IF
    `in a fishing boat` AND `had poison or explosive` AND (NOT `held a licence`)

§§ `12 -- trawl-nets`

-- s 12(1): "No person shall use, operate or assist in the operation of a trawl-net in the territorial waters of Singapore."
-- (2): "imprisonment for a presumptive minimum term of not less than 3 months and not exceeding 3 years" [15/2019]. No fine.
-- (3): forfeiture of the vessel, net, instrument or appliance used and seized -- the court "shall, on the written application of
-- the Public Prosecutor, make an order for the forfeiture ..., notwithstanding that no person may have been convicted".
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the trawl-net minimum months` IS 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the trawl-net maximum months` IS 36

GIVEN `used or assisted with a trawl-net` IS A BOOLEAN, `in territorial waters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trawling is an offence under section 12` IF
    `used or assisted with a trawl-net` AND `in territorial waters`

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is within the section 12(2) range` IF
    `months` AT LEAST `the trawl-net minimum months` AND `months` AT MOST `the trawl-net maximum months`

-- `anyone convicted` is a parameter so the cases can show it makes no difference.
GIVEN `the gear was used in the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the gear was seized by an officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Public Prosecutor applied in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `anyone convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must forfeit the gear` IF
    `the gear was used in the offence` AND `the gear was seized by an officer` AND `the Public Prosecutor applied in writing`

§§ `13 -- penalties`

-- s 13(1), (2): "if no special penalty is provided", a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
-- (2) reaches whoever "does or attempts to do or causes or permits to be done or abets" a contravention, or breaches licence
-- conditions.
-- (3): continuing after conviction -- "for every day during which the offence continues a fine not exceeding $50, and where the
-- offence continues for a period exceeding 10 days after conviction ... imprisonment not exceeding 6 months".
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the general maximum fine` IS 10000

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the general maximum months` IS 12

GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum continuing fine` IS 50 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum continuing months` IS
    IF `days continued after conviction` GREATER THAN 10 THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `15 -- proceeds of seized fish`

-- s 15(1): seized fish "may be sold immediately"; (2): proceeds "held to abide the result of any prosecution or claim"; (3): "Where
-- there is no prosecution or claim, the proceeds of sale shall be paid to the person from whom the fish was seized and if that
-- person cannot be ascertained, the proceeds of sale shall be paid to the Agency."
DECLARE ProceedsGoTo IS ONE OF
    `held to abide the result`
    `the person from whom the fish was seized`
    `the Agency`

GIVEN `there is a prosecution or claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `that person can be ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A ProceedsGoTo
DECIDE `where the proceeds go` IS
    IF `there is a prosecution or claim` THEN `held to abide the result`
    ELSE IF `that person can be ascertained`
         THEN `the person from whom the fish was seized`
         ELSE `the Agency`

§§ `17, 19, 20 -- liability of partners, employers and officers`

-- s 17: licensed partners are each liable for the act or omission of the others "unless he proves to the satisfaction of the court
-- that he had no knowledge of, OR that he in no way directly or indirectly contributed to," it. Either proof is enough.
GIVEN `licence granted to partners` IS A BOOLEAN, `another partner committed the act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the partner is liable under section 17` IF
        `licence granted to partners` AND `another partner committed the act`
    AND (NOT (`proved no knowledge` OR `proved no contribution`))

-- s 19: the employer "shall also be guilty ... unless the employer proves ... (a) that he used diligence to secure compliance with
-- this Act; AND (b) that the offence was committed without his knowledge, consent or connivance." Both proofs are needed.
GIVEN `employee offended in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved diligence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no knowledge, consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is guilty under section 19` IF
    `employee offended in the course of employment` AND (NOT (`proved diligence` AND `proved no knowledge, consent or connivance`))

-- s 20: where a body corporate, partnership or unincorporated association offends, any "director, manager, partner, secretary or
-- other similar officer", or one "purporting to act in any such capacity", is also guilty unless he proves (a) no knowledge,
-- consent or connivance "and" (b) all due diligence. Both proofs are needed.
GIVEN `the body offended` IS A BOOLEAN, `was or purported to be an officer then` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved diligence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no knowledge, consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty under section 20` IF
        `the body offended` AND `was or purported to be an officer then`
    AND (NOT (`proved diligence` AND `proved no knowledge, consent or connivance`))

§§ `18 -- composition`

-- s 18(1): the Director-General "may, in his discretion, compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding $1,000". (2): the Minister prescribes by rules. (3): on payment, no
-- further proceedings.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition is within section 18` IF
    `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum` AT MOST 1000

§§ `22 -- offences outside territorial waters`

-- s 22: "any offence under this Act (other than subsidiary legislation made thereunder) committed outside the territorial waters"
-- by "(a) citizens of Singapore; (b) persons ordinarily resident in Singapore; or (c) the crew or owners of fishing vessels
-- registered in Singapore whether or not the crew or owners are citizens ... or resident" is triable in Singapore as if committed
-- there.
DECLARE Offender HAS
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is ordinarily resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is crew or owner of a Singapore-registered fishing vessel` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the offender` IS AN Offender, `the offence is under subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence abroad is triable in Singapore` IF
        (NOT `the offence is under subsidiary legislation`)
    AND (   `the offender`'s `is a citizen`
         OR `the offender`'s `is ordinarily resident`
         OR `the offender`'s `is crew or owner of a Singapore-registered fishing vessel`)

§§ `25 -- exemption`

-- s 25(1): the Director-General may, "with the approval of the Minister", exempt "absolutely or conditionally" (a) "any person
-- attached to a scientific institution who fishes only for the purposes of scientific research"; or (b) "any person who fishes for
-- personal consumption".
DECLARE Fisher IS ONE OF
    `a researcher at a scientific institution fishing only for research`
    `a researcher who also sells part of the catch`
    `a person fishing for the table`
    `a commercial fisherman`

GIVEN `the fisher` IS A Fisher, `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may exempt` IF
    `the Minister approved` AND
        CONSIDER `the fisher`
        WHEN `a researcher at a scientific institution fishing only for research` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a person fishing for the table` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
